{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA non-blocking PASS under either engine earns the same certification: a signed plan-review attestation that the claim gate, close gate, `review-plan --status` and `sign-review` accept (ADR 0049). Since [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot], an agentic PASS is signed through the same `_finalize_signature` → `attest.sign_plan_review` path, and every agentic verdict carries `coverage.engine = \"agentic\"`; pipeline verdicts carry no `engine` key. The signed manifest does not record which engine produced it, so the two engines cannot be audited side by side once sidecars are pruned (`sidecar.prune`, 50 per ticket).\n\n## Approach\n\n**Signed field.** `manifest.build_manifest` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:478`) appends `engine: <name>` when the verdict's `coverage.engine` is set and is not `\"pipeline\"`. A pipeline manifest is byte-identical to today's, so no existing or future pipeline attestation changes. The line is inside the signed bytes (the signature binds `(ticket_id, manifest)`), so editing it breaks verification. Manifest readers already ignore unknown lines (`manifest.py:14`), so claim, close, `--status` and `sign-review` accept the new line unchanged. New reader `manifest_engine(manifest) -> str` returns the line's value, or `\"pipeline\"` when absent, so every attestation signed before this change reads as pipeline. No migration.\n\n**Carried through every re-sign.**\n- `sign-review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py`) rebuilds the verdict from the stored sidecar, including its `coverage` (`resign.py:337`), and calls `build_manifest`. The agentic sidecar's `coverage.engine` therefore reaches the re-signed manifest with no resign change. A test pins it.\n- `attest.refresh_attestation` (drift refresh) rebuilds the verdict from the prior manifest's fields. It gains `fields[\"coverage\"][\"engine\"] = manifest_engine(prior_manifest)`, so a refreshed agentic attestation keeps its engine. `attest.py` is 786 lines, so this is one line plus the import, and the reader lives in `manifest.py` (709 lines).\n\n**Surfaced.** `attest_gate.plan_review_status` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:202`) adds `engine`: the signed attestation's `manifest_engine`, or `None` when no readable certified attestation exists, beside `currency_basis`. This one function backs the CLI `review-plan --status` JSON and the MCP `plan_review_status` tool. `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json` gains the optional `engine` property (`\"pipeline\"`, `\"agentic\"` or null). It stays out of `required`, so older readers are unaffected. `docs/plan-review-gate.md` documents the field.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py (`engine:` line, `manifest_engine`)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py (refresh carries engine)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py (status field)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll tests run offline with a counting FakeRunner and real signing in a temp repo.\n\n- Happy path: an agentic PASS signs a manifest containing `engine: agentic`. `plan_review_status` reports `certified` with `engine == \"agentic\"`, and `claim` succeeds.\n- Re-sign: after the reviewed code drifts, `sign-review` re-certifies the agentic attestation, and the new manifest still carries `engine: agentic`. `refresh_attestation` on an agentic prior manifest also keeps it.\n- Back-compat: a pipeline PASS manifest has no `engine:` line, is byte-identical to the manifest built without the change, and reads as `\"pipeline\"`. `plan_review_status` reports `engine == \"pipeline\"`.\n- Tamper: rewriting `engine: agentic` to `engine: pipeline` in a signed record fails `signing.verify_signature`.\n- Refusal: an agentic BLOCK and an agentic INDETERMINATE write no attestation, and `engine` is `None` on status.\n- The MCP `plan_review_status` output validates against `plan_review_status.schema.json` with the field present.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Agentic PASS attestations record `engine: agentic` inside the signed manifest. Claim, `review-plan --status`, `sign-review` and drift refresh accept and preserve it, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py`.\n- [ ] Pipeline manifests are byte-identical, and pre-existing attestations without the line read as `\"pipeline\"`, pinned by the back-compat test.\n- [ ] Tampering with the field fails signature verification, pinned by the tamper test.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794455723405107877,"uuid":"a3452c2d-dd43-43d6-8088-f786e38f5967"}